# Shell scripts that run *inside* the Linux container must keep LF endings.
# Without this, a clone on Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to
# CRLF and the container fails at startup with the classic and very
# unhelpful `exec /app/docker/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory`
# (the "missing file" is really the interpreter `/usr/bin/env bash\r`).
# The Dockerfile strips CRs defensively too, but fixing it at the source is
# what keeps a Windows checkout honest.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers stay CRLF so they open cleanly in Notepad.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
